tipsy roll seems simple enough that  piece of gooey chocolate wrapped up in a  perfect little bite but believe it or  not these tasty treats save the lives of  US Marines in the Korean War in 1950 at  the North Korean Chosun reservoir US  Marine troops were engaged in battle the  Marines are running out of ammunition  and called for an airdrop of 16  millimeter mortar rounds codename for  these bullets tootsie roll when the  supplies fell from the sky troops were  surprised to find boxes filled with the  actual candies where the bullets this  fluke turned out to be a blessing in  disguise freezing cold temperatures had  cracked vehicle fuel lines leaving  troops stranded and although the candies  were frozen they softened easily in the  mouths of servicemen so good Marines  quickly realized they can melt the  candies down to a putty and seal the  broken pipes good as new  when the chocolate reef rose they were  able to drive to safety in their newly  functional vehicles the Marines to  successfully escape the reservoir admit  that tootsie rolls had a big hand in  their survival and they call themselves  the chosen few I'd call that a pretty  sweet victory  you  you
 

